{"id":"c66ed8167757bd74","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-df-zfc-model-omega-model.md","title":"ZFC Model Omega Model","display":"df-zfc-model-omega-model — ZFC Model Omega Model","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-model-omega-model","aliases":["58-df-zfc-model-omega-model"],"display":"df-zfc-model-omega-model — ZFC Model Omega Model","depends_on":["[[58-ax-zfc]]","[[../batch09/58-df-model.md]]","[[58-df-satisfaction.md]]","[[../batch03/58-df-assignment.md]]","[[../batch07/58-df-free-variable.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-model-omega-model"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-model-omega-model</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-model-omega-model — ZFC Model Omega Model"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"58-ax-zfc\">58-ax-zfc</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"923884eb8fe4e61d\" href=\"?note=923884eb8fe4e61d\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-model.md\">../batch09/58-df-model.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"58-df-satisfaction.md\">58-df-satisfaction.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"64f35ba2e87964e0\" href=\"?note=64f35ba2e87964e0\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-assignment.md\">../batch03/58-df-assignment.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"715a32e91161b34f\" href=\"?note=715a32e91161b34f\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-free-variable.md\">../batch07/58-df-free-variable.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,\\mathcal L_\\in,\\mathrm{ZFC},\\varphi_\\omega,v_0,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat},s\\in V\">\\(M,\\mathcal L_\\in,\\mathrm{ZFC},\\varphi_\\omega,v_0,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat},s\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L_\\in\">\\(\\mathcal L_\\in\\)</span> is the fixed pure membership language and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZFC}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZFC}\\)</span> its coded theory</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi_\\omega\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_\\in)\">\\(\\varphi_\\omega\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_\\in)\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{FV}_{\\mathcal L_\\in}(\\varphi_\\omega)\\subseteq\\{v_0\\}\">\\(\\operatorname{FV}_{\\mathcal L_\\in}(\\varphi_\\omega)\\subseteq\\{v_0\\}\\)</span>, and metatheoretically <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi_\\omega(v_0)\">\\(\\varphi_\\omega(v_0)\\)</span> says that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"v_0\">\\(v_0\\)</span> is the least inductive set</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Model}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{Model}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"923884eb8fe4e61d\" href=\"?note=923884eb8fe4e61d\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-model.md\">../batch09/58-df-model.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\\subseteq V^4\">\\(\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\\subseteq V^4\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Assign}\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{Assign}\\subseteq V^2\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Univ}:V\\to V\">\\(\\mathrm{Univ}:V\\to V\\)</span> (typed satisfaction, assignments, and structure carrier)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcModelOmegaModel}_S\\subseteq V\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcModelOmegaModel}_S\\subseteq V\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}model\\text{-}omega\\text{-}model}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcModelOmegaModel}_S(M)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Model}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZFC},\\mathcal L_\\in)\n\\land\\omega\\in\\mathrm{Univ}(M)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\exists\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat},s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(M,\\mathcal L_\\in,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\n\\land\\mathrm{Assign}(M,s)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{42mm}{}\\land\\operatorname{Sat}\n(\\varphi_\\omega,s[v_0\\mapsto\\omega])\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}model\\text{-}omega\\text{-}model}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcModelOmegaModel}_S(M)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Model}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZFC},\\mathcal L_\\in)\n\\land\\omega\\in\\mathrm{Univ}(M)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\exists\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat},s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(M,\\mathcal L_\\in,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\n\\land\\mathrm{Assign}(M,s)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{42mm}{}\\land\\operatorname{Sat}\n(\\varphi_\\omega,s[v_0\\mapsto\\omega])\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The external set <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega\">\\(\\omega\\)</span> itself must lie in the structure and satisfy the fixed internal least-inductive-set formula. This expands the former undeclared term <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega^M\">\\(\\omega^M\\)</span> through the registered satisfaction recursion.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-zfc","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"r